3. SCOPE OF MODIFICATION
================================================================================

- The upstream React console (formerly in web/) is preserved, byte-for-byte and
  unmodified, under legacy/upstream-web/ as a frozen reference snapshot. Its
  upstream copyright and Apache-2.0 per-file headers are retained intact.

- The new OwnRAG console in web/ is a separate work that consumes the preserved
  backend's existing HTTP contract (/api/v1/* and /v1/*). New OwnRAG source
  files state that they are "Derived from RAGFlow" and retain the Apache-2.0
  terms.

- The backend and tooling (internal/, cmd/, rag/, docker/, sdk/, conf/, and the
  root build files) are NOT modified; capability preservation is the point of
  the fork.

See DERIVED-WORK.md for the full, file-level statement of what was changed,
moved, added, and preserved.

